BT 1 0 0 1 0 58 Tm /F2+0 9.5 Tf 13.5 TL (Using synthetic matrices makes it possible to change one property at a time while keeping the rest) Tj T* (of the problem under control. This is important because a change in matrix size, sparsity,) Tj T* (conditioning, regularisation, sparsity pattern or spectral distribution changes the numerical problem) Tj T* (itself. The resulting runtime and convergence behaviour therefore cannot be interpreted) Tj T* (independently of those settings.) Tj T* ET
